<!--
  PLAYER pause glyph - official Google Material.

  Source: Material Symbols Rounded `pause`, FILL 0, wght 400, GRAD 0, opsz 24,
  from github.com/google/material-design-icons @ master,
  `symbols/web/pause/materialsymbolsrounded/pause_24px.svg`
  (Apache License 2.0). The pathData below is that file's, verbatim.

  The same family, style, axes and nominal size as ic_player_play.xml, which is
  the whole point of taking the pair from one set rather than pairing two
  drawings: play and pause only look like one control's two faces if the same
  hand drew them at the same weight. See that file for the owner decision this
  implements, for the viewBox translation, and for why no offset or scale is
  applied to either glyph.

  FILL 0, so the two bars are hollow like the stroked pair they replace - the
  inner contours are wound against the outer ones and the default nonZero rule
  opens them. Both drawables share `player_play_glyph_size` so the nominal size
  cannot drift apart, and both are drawn by `scaleType=center` in the 80x80
  control whose fill is the button's own background.
-->
